{"record_id": "entry-522", "entry_number": 522, "status": "complete", "title": "Trump Entertainment Resorts Files Chapter 11 (2009)", "description_short": "Trump Entertainment Resorts Files Chapter 11 (2009)", "description_medium": "Trump Entertainment Resorts filed for Chapter 11 bankruptcy protection in February 2009 after debts accumulated and interest payments were missed. The filing involved multiple Trump-branded casinos in Atlantic City. It was a corporate bankruptcy in the casino group, rather than evidence of a personal bankruptcy by Trump, and reflected financial stress within the business.", "description_long": "Trump Entertainment Resorts filed for Chapter 11 bankruptcy protection in February 2009. The casino group's debts and missed interest payments provided the immediate financial context. Multiple Trump-branded casinos in Atlantic City were involved in the filing, making the event a business-group restructuring rather than an isolated problem at an unnamed property. Chapter 11 protection concerns a company's attempt to deal with obligations through a court-supervised bankruptcy process. The corporate filing should not be rewritten as a personal bankruptcy by Trump. The branding connects the business to his public identity, but it does not erase the distinction between an individual and the corporate entities that entered the proceedings. It does not establish the final recovery for every creditor, the terms of all later transactions or that the bankruptcy itself proved fraudulent conduct. The event documents another episode of financial distress in the Trump casino business, with its legal and corporate scope preserved.", "category": "Grift / Financial Exploitation", "subcategory": "Casino Debt / Bankruptcy", "topic_tags": ["Trump Entertainment Resorts", "Chapter 11", "bankruptcy", "Atlantic City", "casinos"], "people_tags": ["Donald Trump"], "organization_tags": [], "source_urls": ["https://money.cnn.com/2009/02/17/news/companies/trump_entertainment/index.htm"], "preserved_fields": ["title", "description_short"], "notes": ["Reviewed the event account and retained its supported details."], "revision": 2, "supersedes_file": "chatgpt-web/outputs/worker-2-batch-016.jsonl", "revision_reason": "Reviewed generated text against event facts; removed source-audit framing and preserved populated descriptions."}
