{"record_id": "expanded-20260917-trump-axios-annihilate", "entry_number": null, "status": "needs_context", "title": "Trump says he is weighing whether to annihilate Iran's regime", "description_short": "Trump says he is weighing whether to annihilate Iran's regime", "description_medium": "In an Axios interview, Trump said he was approaching a major decision about restarting large-scale attacks and used annihilation language about the Iranian regime. He declined to say whether the decision would come before or after the midterms, while officials described an unresolved military stalemate.", "description_long": "In a September 17, 2026 Axios interview, Trump said he was approaching a major decision about restarting large-scale attacks on Iran. He used annihilation language about the Iranian regime, while declining to say whether the decision would be made before or after the midterm elections. The reported remarks therefore conveyed a threat and pending decision rather than an announced new operation. Officials described the military situation as an unresolved stalemate. That context helps explain the significance of discussing renewed large-scale attacks, but it does not establish that those attacks were ordered or carried out as a result of the interview. It does not settle the eventual choice, the precise military plan or the outcome of any later escalation. The event is the dated interview and its stated decision posture, with future actions left distinct from the president's rhetoric.", "category": "Foreign Policy", "subcategory": null, "topic_tags": ["Iran"], "people_tags": ["Donald Trump"], "organization_tags": ["White House", "Axios"], "source_urls": ["https://www.axios.com/2026/09/17/trump-axios-interview-iran-war"], "preserved_fields": ["title", "description_short", "description_medium"], "notes": ["M", "i", "s", "s", "i", "n", "g", " ", "d", "e", "s", "c", "r", "i", "p", "t", "i", "o", "n", "s", " ", "c", "o", "m", "p", "o", "s", "e", "d", " ", "f", "r", "o