{"record_id": "entry-6796", "entry_number": 6796, "status": "needs_context", "title": "DOJ Freezes Civil Rights Division Litigation Pending Trump Administration Review", "description_short": "DOJ Freezes Civil Rights Division Litigation Pending Trump Administration Review", "description_medium": "The Justice Department ordered a halt to new and ongoing Civil Rights Division litigation and settlements while cases were reviewed. The evidence does not support the claim that the entire senior leadership was placed on leave on January 21 or that the division ceased to function.", "description_long": "The Justice Department ordered a halt to new and ongoing Civil Rights Division litigation and settlements while reviewing the cases. Reuters reported the internal directive on January 22, 2025. The documented action concerned the division's legal work during an administration transition, with decisions about proceeding placed under review. A pause in litigation is significant because it affects the handling of matters already underway as well as proposed new cases. It should nevertheless be described according to its actual scope. Those broader personnel and shutdown claims would require separate evidence. The litigation directive alone also does not determine the outcome of every affected case or establish that each review resulted in abandonment. The supported account is a departmental restriction on litigation and settlements, rather than a claim that the whole division was dismantled in a single action.", "category": "Authoritarianism", "subcategory": null, "topic_tags": [], "people_tags": ["Pam Bondi", "Donald Trump"], "organization_tags": [], "source_urls": ["https://www.reuters.com/world/us/us-justice-dept-asks-civil-rights-division-halt-biden-era-litigation-washington-2025-01-22/"], "preserved_fields": ["title", "description_short", "description_medium"], "notes": ["M", "i", "s", "s", "i", "n", "g", " ", "d", "e", "s", "c", "r", "i", "p", "t", "i", "o", "n", "s", " "